The list literal generated for the "items" prefix already requires as
many elements as "minItems" does, so no list.MinItems constraint is
generated, and with it goes the only use of the list package.

-- schema.json --
{
    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
    "type": "array",
    "items": [
        {"type": "integer"},
        {"type": "string"}
    ],
    "minItems": 2
}
-- test/exact.json --
[1, "a"]
-- test/longer.json --
[1, "a", true]
-- test/err-too-short.json --
[1]
-- test/err-wrong-type.json --
["a", "b"]
-- out/decode/extract --
@jsonschema(schema="http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#")

[int, string, ...]
-- out/decode/testerr/err-too-short --
incompatible list lengths (1 and 2):
    test/err-too-short.json:1:1
-- out/decode/testerr/err-wrong-type --
0: conflicting values int and "a" (mismatched types int and string):
    generated.cue:3:1
    generated.cue:3:2
    test/err-wrong-type.json:1:2
